## Vendored code

The analysis and report code in `engine/` and the dashboard template in
`assets/dashboard.html` are vendored from the dsh-session-insights project and
remain under its MIT license:

- Upstream project: dsh-session-insights, https://github.com/GreenLv/dsh-session-insights
- Copyright (c) 2026 Gerui Lv
- License: MIT

`engine/reader.js` (host session-log discovery and snapshot selection) and
`engine/facet-cache.js` (the cross-run facet cache) are maintained by this
skill, not vendored, and carry this license.

The report schema in `engine/report.schema.json` is the upstream report schema
v1 with this skill's product and schema identifiers:

- Upstream file: docs/schema/report-v1.schema.json

Adaptations made for this skill: the report's product and schema identifiers,
the run-directory marker product id, the dashboard template path, the
branding strings in the dashboard template, and the meta-analysis detection
patterns that recognize this skill. Analysis behaviour is unchanged.

The closed facet vocabulary in `engine/rules.js` (the goal categories, outcome,
satisfaction, helpfulness, session type, friction and success sets, together
with their wording) is shared with Claude Code's `/insights` facet schema,
Copyright (c) Anthropic PBC, used here under the MIT license of the
claude-code source distribution. Vendor words in that vocabulary are renamed to
this runtime's assistant terms in shipped code.

## Host libraries

The engine reads session logs through the DeepSeek Harness host libraries at
run time, which are MIT licensed:

- `@deepseek-ai/dsh-session-query` — https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness
- `@deepseek-ai/dsh-session-persistence` — https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness
- `@deepseek-ai/dsh-session-persistence-jsonl` — https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness
- `@deepseek-ai/dsh-session` — https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness
- `@deepseek-ai/cordis` — https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness
